[[Lore:Calcelmo's Stone|Calcelmo's Stone]] is an artifact bearing inscriptions in both the [[Lore:Dwemer Alphabet|Dwemer]] and [[Lore:Falmer Alphabet|Falmer]] alphabets. It was owned by [[Lore:Calcelmo|Calcelmo]], the court wizard of [[Lore:Markarth|Markarth]] circa {{Year|4E 201}} and one of the most recognizable [[Lore:Dwemer|Dwemer]] scholars at the time.{{Ref|name=SRCalcelmo|[[Skyrim:Calcelmo|Calcelmo]]'s dialogue in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} The stone was kept in his tower in [[Lore:Understone Keep|Understone Keep]] and under heavy protection.{{Ref|name=SREnthir|[[Skyrim:Enthir|Enthir]]'s dialogue in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}{{Ref|name=SRAnswers|[[Skyrim:Hard Answers|Hard Answers]] faction quest in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}<noinclude> 

When Calcelmo acquired the stone is unknown. Sometime before his death in {{Year|4E 176}},{{Ref|name=SRKarliah|[[Skyrim:Karliah#Hard Answers|Karliah]]'s dialogue in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} the Guildmaster of the [[Lore:Thieves Guild|Thieves Guild]], [[Lore:Gallus Desidenius|Gallus Desidenius]] infiltrated Calcelmo's Tower and used the stone to learn the Falmer language after receiving a tip from a friend in [[Lore:Winterhold (city)|Winterhold]].{{Ref|name=SREnthir}} Years later while trying to follow his trail, another [[Lore:Last Dragonborn|member]] of the Thieves Guild entered the tower and took a rubbing of the stone to translate Gallus' journal.{{Ref|name=SRAnswers}}
{{NewLeft}}

